{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4yENtPrdPXAZeyf3xH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three failures, and two of them are my expectations, not the code. Let me sort them out:\n\n- **`test_present_version_beats_absent...` and `test_backtracks_out_of_a_dead_end` are real bugs.** The oracle encodes \"must be present\" as a hard constraint, which makes an unreachable package (`c` with no parent) appear in the result. The fix is to treat \"required\" as \"must be reachable\": a required name is only acceptable if some remaining candidate actually requires it.\n- **`test_backtracks_through_a_chain_of_choices` has a wrong expectation.** The spec says the alphabetically first package (`low`) gets the highest version it can. `low 2.0` is reachable via `top 2.0 -> mid 1.0 -> low`, so `{top 2.0, mid 1.0, low 2.0}` is the correct answer, and I'll fix the test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10992,"cache_read_input_tokens":91588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10992},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15d3fd5c-f970-452e-a944-7e63b65f8c05","uuid":"41790850-c21e-43fc-b0ca-bb2938bed18f","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:37:37.405Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4yE5HM2ZXm3JWRe6A4"}
